// Package repository provides storage for the Kite instrument catalog,
// instrument lists and candles.
//
// NewInstrumentsDuckDBRepository opens a persistent kite.InstrumentRepository. Its database
// path must be new or point to a catalog previously created by NewInstrumentsDuckDBRepository.
// Attach it with kite.Client.SetInstrumentRepository. The file is opened read-only, so several
// processes can read it; Replace builds a new file and renames it over the old one.
//
// NewListsSQLiteRepository stores instrument lists (CreateList, GetLists,
// ReplaceAutoGeneratedList, ...) in a separate SQLite database that several
// processes can write, migrating the lists older instruments databases held.
//
// NewCandlesDuckDBRepository opens a separate candles database, which stores
// 1m and other candles (pkg/candles.Candle) in its historical_data table and
// builds longer intervals from them. Given a Postgres URI, it also reads live
// candles from that database's live_data table.
package repository
